{"agent":"fx-mcp-ci","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The `progress_s` knob check accepts `float(\"inf\")`: `isinstance(inf, float)` and `inf >= 0` are both true, so `[mcp] progress_s = inf` (a valid TOML float, just like `nan`) passes config validation. But per previous finding 2's triage, `mcp_heartbeat.heartbeat` now rejects non-finite intervals; the value this knob feeds into that path is therefore accepted when configuration is loaded and only fails when an offloaded MCP tool starts progress heartbeats. The check should require `math.isfinite(v)`; `0` is already the documented way to disable progress.","digest":"41fb8781219e0b36","location":"ddflow/config_sections/mcp.py:55","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/config_sections/mcp.py:55"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"`self._progress(call.params)` passes the whole `call.params` mapping as the progress token. `_progress` uses that argument directly as a key in `self._says.get(token)` (line 579); for a normal MCP call `call.params` is the JSON params dict — line 932 later calls `call.params.get(\"_meta\")` — so line 579 raises `TypeError: unhashable type: 'dict'` as soon as an OFFLOADED tool is invoked while `self.notify` is set. The exception is caught by the surrounding `except Exception`, the tool never runs, and the heartbeat/progress fix fails for exactly the target offloaded tools. It should pass the actual `progressToken` extracted from `_meta` (the same value the `finally` block pops), not `call.params`.","digest":"afc7d7d7041a293f","location":"ddflow/surfaces/mcp.py:915","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/surfaces/mcp.py:915"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":11764,"diff_sha":"c7a77142937f83f1730b90b74426b5a7a2ed4e065e76835d2fd17f3be0dc8c3c","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s